llvm-4.0.0 backport patch: one nop after every call to __stack_chk_fail (PS4)

This patch CHANGES CODE GENERATION for every function that carries a stack
canary: the call to __stack_chk_fail in the protector's failure block is
followed by a one-byte nop, as the PS4 compiler emits it in both of its
generations (the library region's 751 calls, the game region's 5,981: every
one is followed by 0x90, no other callee is; the function's unwind range
includes the byte; 5,899 game functions end with it). It is the game
line's form of tools/patches/llvm-3.3-sspnop-01-stack-chk-fail-nop.patch,
which docs/DECISIONS.md D26 ruled for both lines on 2026-10-27 and left
for the day the game line was a source build (D45). The unpatched line
ends such a function at the call. In 4.0 the failure call is a libcall
of the stack protector's lowering, an external symbol, where 3.3 called
the declared function: the test takes both. No matched game row carries
a canary, so none changes; 0x1354ee0 compiles to the base's bytes.

--- a/lib/Target/X86/X86MCInstLower.cpp
+++ b/lib/Target/X86/X86MCInstLower.cpp
@@ -1731,6 +1731,22 @@
     SMShadowTracker.emitShadowPadding(*OutStreamer, getSubtargetInfo());
     // Then emit the call
     OutStreamer->EmitInstruction(TmpInst, getSubtargetInfo());
+
+    // The PS4 compiler follows every call to __stack_chk_fail with one nop,
+    // in both of its generations, so that the return address of the failure
+    // call stays inside the calling function (docs/DECISIONS.md D26: 751 of
+    // 751 such calls in the library region, 5,981 of 5,981 in the game).
+    // The call is a libcall of the stack protector's lowering (an external
+    // symbol) or, from the IR-level failure block, a call of the declared
+    // function (a global).
+    const MachineOperand &Callee = MI->getOperand(0);
+    if (MI->getOpcode() == X86::CALL64pcrel32 &&
+        ((Callee.isSymbol() &&
+          StringRef(Callee.getSymbolName()) == "__stack_chk_fail") ||
+         (Callee.isGlobal() &&
+          Callee.getGlobal()->getName() == "__stack_chk_fail")))
+      OutStreamer->EmitInstruction(MCInstBuilder(X86::NOOP),
+                                   getSubtargetInfo());
     return;
   }
 
